  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 49a9dd75b14f64f43a98b9b523c7ac90, type: 3}
  m_Name: BobCubicle
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueObject
  _concurrentDialogue:
  - Bob the builder is what we all used to call him. He hated the nickname but no
    one stopped. He came to accept it and embrace it even.
  - "He was, or is, I\u2019m not sure if he\u2019s still alive. Bob was very hardworking."
  - He had a wife and 3 kids from what I recall. All he ever did was gush about his
    family when he had the time.
  - But whenever it was time to work, he would get very serious. He felt like the
    big brother of the team.
  - He was the only one to notice what was happening between Marcy and I. I never
    confirmed it to him, so he was only going off a hunch.
  - He would also always try to ease the tension between Dan and I.
  - "When Felicity and Cindy wanted to celebrate and drink, he would only stay for
    about half an hour and go home. \u201CMy family is waiting for me\u201D is what
    he would say. He even brought his wife to one of the outings and presented her
    to us. They seemed to be fulfilled and happy with their life."
  - "At some point I envied what he had, but I was also happy for him. When Cindy
    died, he was the first to quit and said he had to get his family out of the country\u2026"
  - "He took everything, leaving his cubicle empty\u2026"
  - "I wonder where you are now Bob\u2026"
  - "I hope you and your family are okay and happy as ever\u2026"
  _characterName: You
  _nextDialogue: {fileID: 0}
